# Scan Kit 2

Follow [docs/software/architecture.md](docs/software/architecture.md).

Pliant (product SK) is the source of truth for intended use, safety classification, requirements, hazards, traceability, test plans, defects, releases, and the SOUP list. Read and update them there with the Pliant tools. Do not add compliance documents to the repository; engineering guides and design notes stay here.

- Domain behavior lives in `scan-kit-core` once. Session files and the sqlite store live in `scan-kit-io`. GPU work uses `wgpu` only. Plot drawing lives in `scan-kit-plot`, which also builds to wasm32 for the webview. Do not draw plots in TypeScript or ship frames over the Tauri bridge. Compute kernels live in `scan-kit-compute`. Register each operation on that crate's tool catalog. `scan-kit-mcp` and Tauri commands call that function. They do not reimplement it.
- Workflow tools call granular functions in process.
- Desktop chrome stays on the stock shadcn dark theme from [ui.shadcn.com](https://ui.shadcn.com/) (`base-nova`, Base UI). Tabular data uses Glide Data Grid, themed from the stock tokens. Add chrome with `npx shadcn add <name>` in `apps/desktop` and use that file as written. Do not hand-write a select, input, button, checkbox, dialog, menu, tabs, or label, and do not restyle a copied component. Do not edit theme tokens, add custom color, radius, type, or spacing CSS, or add another component library for chrome. Do not add a shadcn Table for data.
- Pull requests target `develop`.
- The Scan Kit SOUP list in Pliant (SK-DOC-3, or the product SBOM once imported) is refreshed at release time, not per pull request. Dependency changes accumulate between releases; update the SOUP list when cutting a release.
- While editing Rust or desktop code, check the crate you changed, following [.cursor/skills/static-analysis/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/static-analysis/SKILL.md). Run that skill's full list once before the pull request. Do not silence a lint with `#[allow]` or an Oxlint disable, and do not skip a failing test to get green.
- A plot change reads the module docs at the top of `crates/scan-kit-plot/src/render.rs` first: paint order is shared by the GPU pass, the CPU fallback, and hover, and a mark's byte layout is spread across its stride, attributes, encoder, decoder, and WGSL inputs.
